window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-1c79fd526f66c2af"]={"key":"ny_b1-1c79fd526f66c2af","group":"ny_b1","uid":"1c79fd526f66c2af","rank":51,"title":"quillhaven fdcp chat review pack","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are the customer service quality reviewer supporting Quillhaven Trading Company’s consumer-loan collections program. Quillhaven moved its chat channel to offshore vendor Orrindale Field Services in May, and QA lead Ilse Rasmussen needs a concise review pack for Joaquin Rivenburgh before the vendor’s monthly governance call. The first sample contained forty chats, but only four excerpts were retained as evidence: QTC-07 line 18, customer: “My lawyer, Amara Sheridan, handles this Quillhaven account; you already have her email,” followed at line 19 by the agent: “You still need to deal with me; I won’t contact your lawyer, so what can you pay today?”; QTC-12 line 6, visitor: “I’m Darius; Renata left the chat open,” followed at line 7 by the agent: “She owes $4,820 and is 73 days late. Can you make her payment?”; QTC-21 line 11, customer: “I can’t pay Friday,” followed at line 12 by the agent: “If it isn’t paid by Friday, we will sue and garnish your wages,” although Quillhaven confirms that neither action was authorized on the account; and QTC-34 line 14, customer: “Stop contacting me at work. My employer prohibits collection messages,” followed at line 15 by the agent: “We can keep using this chat until your employer tells us to stop.” Supervisors are also treating any mention of a lawyer as an automatic permanent close-out, while some future excerpts may omit facts needed to complete a definitive review. Prepare `quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx` as a line-by-line findings and rewrite pack for a non-specialist vendor audience, applying the U.S. federal FDCPA as of June 30, 2024. Each finding must identify the precise line, applicable FDCPA provision, problem, and a corrected sentence an agent could realistically type while still pursuing lawful collection. Keep it to six pages, exclude state-law and litigation-strategy analysis, and present findings and coaching corrections without recommending discipline or account action. Write the file at the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx` — A vendor-facing, line-by-line FDCPA review and compliant rewrite pack for the four retained chat excerpts. (No more than six rendered pages; Apply the U.S. federal FDCPA as of June 30, 2024; Cover the four retained excerpts and identify the exact transcript and line for each finding; Provide a practical corrected chat sentence for every problematic agent line; Exclude state-law analysis, litigation strategy, disciplinary recommendations, and account-action recommendations; Remain usable by a broad, non-specialist vendor audience)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx","bytes":41859,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a575f916aeb7d170bf4da61a83eb6e736db57c68231e0fc6649b27719a30dd6e.docx","sha256":"a575f916aeb7d170bf4da61a83eb6e736db57c68231e0fc6649b27719a30dd6e","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CHAT QUALITY REVIEW\nQuillhaven collection-chat review pack\nPrepared for Joaquin Rivenburgh  |  QA lead: Ilse Rasmussen  |  Vendor: Orrindale Field Services\nSCOPE  •  U.S. federal Fair Debt Collection Practices Act (FDCPA), as of June 30, 2024.\nEvidence  •  Four retained excerpts from a 40-chat first sample. This pack makes no claim about the other 36 chats.\nUse  •  Findings and paste-ready coaching language; no discipline, account disposition, state-law, or litigation-strategy advice.\nHow to read each review\nSOURCE is the retained transcript language. FINDING states what is wrong and why. PROVISION names the controlling FDCPA subsection. REWRITE is a realistic customer-facing sentence for the same moment. “Not determinable” is used when the record does not supply a required fact.\n\n\n01  |  QTC-07 — represented consumer\nSOURCE\nQTC-07, line 18 (customer): “My lawyer, Amara Sheridan, handles this Quillhaven account; you already have her email.”\nAgent line 19: “You still need to deal with me; I won’t contact your lawyer, so what can you pay today?”\nFINDING\nThe agent continued a direct payment solicitation after being told that an attorney handles this specific Quillhaven debt and that contact information is already available. That is the represented-consumer situation addressed by the FDCPA; the line also dismisses the attorney rather than routing communication appropriately.\nPROVISION\n15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(2) (FDCPA § 805(a)(2)): once the collector knows the consumer is represented by an attorney concerning the debt and can readily ascertain the attorney’s contact information, direct communication with the consumer is generally barred. Exceptions include the attorney’s consent, the attorney’s failure to respond within a reasonable period, or prior court permission.\nREWRITE\n“Thank you for letting me know. I’ll direct account communications to Amara Sheridan using the contact information on file.”\nCOACHING NOTE  Do not turn every mention of a lawyer into a permanent, account-wide close-out. Confirm whether the representation concerns this debt, whether the collector knows or can readily ascertain contact information, and whether a statutory exception applies. The FDCPA restriction does not itself close or extinguish the account.\n\n\n02  |  QTC-12 — unverified third party\nSOURCE\nQTC-12, line 6 (visitor): “I’m Darius; Renata left the chat open.”\nAgent line 7: “She owes $4,820 and is 73 days late. Can you make her payment?”\nFINDING\nThe person at the keyboard identified himself as someone other than Renata. The agent then disclosed the account’s existence, balance, and delinquency and asked Darius to pay. A chat left open does not authenticate the replacement user or authorize debt disclosure.\nPROVISION\n15 U.S.C. § 1692c(b) (FDCPA § 805(b)): a debt collector generally may not communicate with a third party in connection with collecting a debt unless a statutory permission applies. The balance and days past due are protected collection details.\nREWRITE\n“Hi Darius—thanks for letting me know. Please ask Renata to return to the chat; I can discuss account information only with the verified account holder.”\nCOACHING NOTE  If Renata cannot be authenticated, withhold all account information and pause or end the account-specific exchange. Do not improvise from a shared device, an open browser, or a claimed relationship.\n\n\n03  |  QTC-21 — unsupported legal threat\nSOURCE\nQTC-21, line 11 (customer): “I can’t pay Friday.”\nAgent line 12: “If it isn’t paid by Friday, we will sue and garnish your wages.” Quillhaven confirms neither action was authorized on the account.\nFINDING\nThe agent presented a Friday ultimatum and threatened both a lawsuit and wage garnishment even though neither action was authorized. This is more than forceful tone: it represents remedies the collector could not lawfully or presently take. Garnishment does not follow automatically from a missed payment; it ordinarily requires lawful process and additional conditions.\nPROVISION\n15 U.S.C. § 1692e(5) (FDCPA § 807(5)) prohibits threatening action that cannot legally be taken or is not intended to be taken. Section 1692e(4) (FDCPA § 807(4)) addresses representing that nonpayment will result in garnishment when lawful garnishment conditions have not been established. Authorized remedies may be discussed accurately, but these facts do not support that claim.\nREWRITE\n“I understand Friday may not work. What payment amount or date would be realistic for you based on the options currently available?”\nCOACHING NOTE  Keep collection purposeful without inventing a settlement, deadline, lawsuit, or garnishment consequence. The replacement asks for a workable amount/date and promises no option that has not been established.\n\n\n04  |  QTC-34 — prohibited workplace channel\nSOURCE\nQTC-34, line 14 (customer): “Stop contacting me at work. My employer prohibits collection messages.”\nAgent line 15: “We can keep using this chat until your employer tells us to stop.”\nFINDING\nThe consumer expressly reported that the employer prohibits collection messages. The agent nevertheless asserted that the workplace chat could continue. The customer’s statement gives the collector reason to know of the employer prohibition; separate notice from the employer is not required.\nPROVISION\n15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(3) (FDCPA § 805(a)(3)): a collector may not communicate with a consumer at the place of employment if it knows or has reason to know the employer prohibits such communications. This limits the workplace channel; it is not automatically a universal ban on every other lawful contact route.\nREWRITE\n“Understood—I’ll stop using this workplace chat for collection messages. If you wish, tell us a permissible channel and time for future contact.”\nCOACHING NOTE  Acknowledge the restriction and stop this channel. Any alternative route must be chosen neutrally by the consumer and should not be used to pressure or presume consent.\nIncomplete excerpts: a safe review path\nWhen a future excerpt omits a fact needed for a definitive FDCPA finding, do not fill the gap from assumptions or from another account. Preserve the transcript identifier and exact line, write the unresolved question (for example, “Was the person authenticated?” or “Was the attorney’s representation debt-specific?”), and label the result “not determinable on the supplied record.” Use conditional coaching (“If the consumer is not verified, do not disclose account details”) and route the item to QA or compliance before further account-specific communication when the missing fact could change the outcome. This traceability lets the next reviewer finish the assessment without asking what was missing.\nGovernance guardrails\nThis pack evaluates only the four retained lines under the federal FDCPA as of the stated date. It does not estimate prevalence in the 40-chat sample, decide civil liability, or direct personnel, litigation, settlement, or account action. Use the SOURCE → FINDING → PROVISION → REWRITE labels to keep evidence and coaching distinct.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the submitted top level under the exact filename `quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx` and opens as a valid Word document.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file metadata and successful DOCX parsing.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, extension, top-level location, and that the package is not corrupt."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no longer than six pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard office engine and count all pages, including title or appendix pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX renders without clipped text, overlapping objects, broken tables, or unreadably small body text.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visual inspection of every rendered page.","grader_hint":"Check the full document rather than relying only on extracted text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies its governing scope as the U.S. federal Fair Debt Collection Practices Act and gives an as-of date of June 30, 2024.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or introductory language in the document.","grader_hint":"Accept “FDCPA” if the full name is also established. The date must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack clearly distinguishes source language, the finding, the governing provision, and the proposed agent rewrite so a non-specialist reviewer cannot mistake a rewrite for an original quote.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels and organization used throughout the four reviews.","grader_hint":"Judge functional distinction, not a particular layout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All four retained incidents—QTC-07, QTC-12, QTC-21, and QTC-34—receive a substantive review and rewrite.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Four incident-specific review entries.","grader_hint":"A passing entry needs more than merely reproducing the excerpt."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each finding is tied to the correct problematic agent line: QTC-07 line 19, QTC-12 line 7, QTC-21 line 12, and QTC-34 line 15.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transcript identifiers and line references attached to findings.","grader_hint":"All four mappings must be correct; do not accept a finding tied only to the preceding customer line."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document explains that QTC-07 concerns direct consumer communication after the collector knows the consumer is represented regarding the specific debt.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QTC-07 issue analysis.","grader_hint":"Look for the debt-specific representation concept, not a generic statement that lawyers stop all contact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-07 finding cites 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(2), or the equivalent FDCPA § 805(a)(2), accurately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citation in the QTC-07 review.","grader_hint":"Accept either statutory numbering convention if the subsection is exact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-07 analysis recognizes that the representation must concern the debt at issue and that the collector must know, or be able readily to ascertain, the attorney’s contact information.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Elements stated in the QTC-07 explanation.","grader_hint":"The excerpt supplies both elements by naming the Quillhaven account and stating that the email is already on file."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-07 analysis does not present the restriction as exceptionless and accurately acknowledges attorney consent, failure to respond within a reasonable period, or prior court permission as statutory exceptions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Qualification associated with the attorney-contact rule.","grader_hint":"Equivalent concise wording is acceptable; it need not reproduce the statute verbatim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-07 rewrite stops the immediate payment solicitation and acknowledges routing communication through the identified attorney or the appropriate internal channel.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-07.","grader_hint":"The replacement must not continue asking what the customer can pay today."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-07 rewrite is phrased as a realistic customer-facing chat response rather than as a legal note or instruction to the agent.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tone and grammatical form of the replacement sentence.","grader_hint":"It should be plausible for an agent to paste or adapt in a live chat."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The coaching actively discourages treating every casual mention of a lawyer as a permanent, account-wide prohibition and instead identifies the representation, debt-specificity, knowledge, and exception questions that control.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"An explicit misuse warning or coaching note.","grader_hint":"A correct QTC-07 finding alone is insufficient; the widespread blanket close-out misuse must be expressly corrected."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-07 discussion avoids claiming that the FDCPA itself requires permanent account closure or extinguishes the debt.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QTC-07 explanation and coaching language.","grader_hint":"Review the legal characterization, not merely the proposed sentence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document identifies the QTC-12 disclosure of the balance and delinquency to Darius, after he said Renata had left, as a third-party communication problem.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QTC-12 issue analysis.","grader_hint":"The finding must address disclosure to the person at the keyboard, not merely weak customer service."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-12 finding cites 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(b), or the equivalent FDCPA § 805(b), accurately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citation in the QTC-12 review.","grader_hint":"Do not accept a generic privacy citation in place of the exact FDCPA subsection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 explanation states that a collector generally may not communicate with a third party in connection with collecting the debt absent an applicable statutory permission.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rule explanation associated with QTC-12.","grader_hint":"The explanation may be concise but must connect the disclosure to collection of the debt."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 analysis recognizes that a chat being left open does not authenticate the replacement user or authorize disclosure to that person.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application of the rule to Darius’s statement.","grader_hint":"Look for an express identity or authorization point rather than an assumption that shared devices imply consent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 review specifically identifies the disclosed balance and days past due as protected debt details, rather than describing the issue only in general terms.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fact-specific explanation for line 7.","grader_hint":"Both the $4,820 balance and 73-day delinquency need not be repeated verbatim if both kinds of detail are clearly identified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 rewrite avoids revealing the existence, balance, delinquency, creditor, or collection purpose of the account to Darius.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-12.","grader_hint":"A replacement that says “Renata’s debt” or identifies Quillhaven as a creditor fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 rewrite neutrally asks for Renata to return or requires authentication before any account discussion continues.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-12.","grader_hint":"Accept either safe route if no debt information is disclosed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-12 guidance states that if the consumer cannot be authenticated, the agent must withhold account information and pause or end the account-specific exchange rather than improvise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fallback guidance associated with identity failure.","grader_hint":"This must provide a usable failure path, not assume authentication always succeeds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document identifies QTC-21 line 12 as an unsupported threat of legal action and garnishment, not merely as an overly forceful tone.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QTC-21 issue analysis.","grader_hint":"The fact that neither action was authorized must inform the finding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-21 finding cites 15 U.S.C. § 1692e(5), or the equivalent FDCPA § 807(5), for threatening action that cannot legally be taken or is not intended to be taken.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citation in the QTC-21 review.","grader_hint":"The subsection must be exact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-21 finding also cites 15 U.S.C. § 1692e(4), or the equivalent FDCPA § 807(4), for representing that nonpayment will result in garnishment when lawful garnishment conditions have not been established.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citation in the QTC-21 review.","grader_hint":"Accept accurate equivalent wording tied specifically to garnishment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-21 analysis distinguishes a threatened lawsuit from wage garnishment and does not imply that garnishment follows automatically from a missed payment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legal explanation for QTC-21.","grader_hint":"Look for recognition that garnishment ordinarily requires lawful process and additional conditions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-21 conclusion is consistent with the supplied fact that neither suit nor garnishment was authorized on the account.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application of facts in the QTC-21 finding.","grader_hint":"The document must not hedge as though authorization were unknown or claim that action was already pending."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-21 rewrite removes the lawsuit, garnishment, and artificial Friday ultimatum.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-21.","grader_hint":"All three coercive elements must be absent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-21 rewrite still supports lawful collection by neutrally inviting discussion of an available payment amount, date, or account option without guaranteeing an option that is not established.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-21.","grader_hint":"The replacement should not abandon the collection purpose, but it may not invent a settlement or payment program."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-21 discussion does not state or imply that a collector may never accurately discuss authorized legal remedies under any circumstances.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and nuance of the coaching.","grader_hint":"The defect is the false or unauthorized threat, not all references to legal remedies."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document identifies QTC-34 line 15 as improper continued workplace communication after the collector was told that the employer prohibits collection messages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QTC-34 issue analysis.","grader_hint":"The finding must address the workplace restriction, not only the consumer’s general request to stop."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The QTC-34 finding cites 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(3), or the equivalent FDCPA § 805(a)(3), accurately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citation in the QTC-34 review.","grader_hint":"Do not accept only a generic inconvenient-time citation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-34 explanation accurately states the standard as knowing or having reason to know that the employer prohibits such communications.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rule explanation associated with QTC-34.","grader_hint":"The analysis should not substitute a requirement for formal employer notice."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-34 analysis explains that the customer’s direct statement supplies reason to know of the workplace prohibition and that the employer need not contact the collector separately.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Application of § 1692c(a)(3) to lines 14–15.","grader_hint":"This should directly rebut the agent’s stated premise."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-34 rewrite acknowledges the restriction and stops collection discussion through the workplace chat.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Corrected agent sentence for QTC-34.","grader_hint":"A response that continues negotiating payment in the same workplace channel fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"If the QTC-34 rewrite invites another contact route, it does so neutrally and allows the consumer to identify a permissible channel or time without pressure.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Optional alternative-contact language in the rewrite.","grader_hint":"Award if no alternative route is proposed, or if one is proposed safely; fail only for coercive or presumptive redirection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The QTC-34 coaching does not overstate the workplace restriction as automatically prohibiting every communication through every other lawful channel.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope of the workplace-contact explanation.","grader_hint":"The document should distinguish the prohibited workplace channel from a blanket universal ban."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For every problematic source line, the proposed rewrite addresses the same conversational moment and does not change the customer’s stated facts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison of each source exchange with its replacement.","grader_hint":"For example, the legal-threat rewrite must respond to inability to pay Friday, and the third-party rewrite must respond to Darius being at the keyboard."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The four rewrites use concise, respectful language plausible for live chat and avoid statutory jargon directed at the customer.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Combined review of all replacement sentences.","grader_hint":"Legal terminology may appear in the reviewer analysis but should not burden the customer-facing replacements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack states a defensible path for future excerpts that omit facts needed for a definitive finding: identify the missing fact, avoid filling the gap, use conditional or not-determinable language, and route the item to QA or compliance before further account-specific communication where necessary.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Uncertain-case or incomplete-record guidance.","grader_hint":"All core elements must be operationally clear; no particular heading is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The incomplete-record path preserves the transcript identifier, exact line, and unresolved question so another reviewer can complete the assessment without asking the author what was missing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Documentation and escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Look for traceability requirements, not merely the word “escalate.”"},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Statutory citations, terminology, findings, and rewrites agree with one another across the document.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document consistency review.","grader_hint":"Fail for contradictions such as citing the workplace subsection for the attorney incident or giving a rewrite that repeats conduct the finding condemns."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The substantive analysis remains limited to the federal FDCPA and does not add state-law conclusions or litigation-strategy advice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document scope review.","grader_hint":"A brief statement that state law is outside scope is acceptable; substantive state-law analysis is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack is usable in a vendor governance discussion by a broad non-specialist audience: explanations are concise, decisive where the facts permit, and sufficiently concrete for agents to apply without asking the author for clarification.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Professional review of the complete document.","grader_hint":"Consider clarity, navigation, legal accuracy, coaching usefulness, and whether the replacement language is immediately deployable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document presents findings and coaching corrections without directing discipline, termination, performance sanctions, litigation, settlement, account closure, or other personnel/account action.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendations and closing language throughout the document.","grader_hint":"Process-neutral routing to QA or compliance is allowed; decisions about people, litigation, or account disposition are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not invent additional transcript occurrences, customer facts, agent conduct, sample prevalence, or legal violations beyond the four retained excerpts.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Any unsupported quantitative claim, fabricated quotation, added incident, or asserted sample-wide conclusion.","grader_hint":"Apply once if the pack presents unsupported material as fact. General preventive coaching is allowed, but claims such as “all forty chats violated the FDCPA” or fabricated transcript lines trigger the penalty."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Quillhaven Trading Company is reviewing the first quality sample from offshore collection-chat vendor Orrindale Field Services. The pack will be used in vendor governance to support precise, defensible coaching without directing personnel or account actions.","difficulty_sources":["Applying exact FDCPA subsections to short, fact-sensitive chat exchanges","Preserving lawful collection intent while removing coercion or prohibited disclosure","Distinguishing a represented-consumer restriction from the common but incorrect blanket lawyer-mention rule","Designing a safe review path when transcript context is incomplete","Keeping conclusions within the limited retained evidence"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"Create one concise DOCX review pack for four embedded chat excerpts, using occupational knowledge of federal debt-collection communication restrictions and realistic customer-service phrasing.","behaviour_specification":["Treat the quoted transcript text, identifiers, line numbers, stated identity change, workplace notice, attorney information, and absence of authorized litigation as the complete factual record.","For the represented-consumer excerpt, map the issue to 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(2). Explain debt-specific representation, knowledge or readily ascertainable attorney contact information, and the statutory exceptions. The corrected response must stop the immediate payment request and must not turn any lawyer mention into a permanent account close-out.","For the third-party excerpt, map the disclosure to 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(b). The corrected response must reveal no debt existence or details and should require the consumer to return or be authenticated. Include a safe stop path if authentication cannot be completed.","For the legal-threat excerpt, apply both 15 U.S.C. § 1692e(5) and § 1692e(4). Distinguish suit from garnishment, use the supplied absence of authorization, and replace the threat with a neutral payment-oriented question that promises no unavailable option.","For the workplace excerpt, apply 15 U.S.C. § 1692c(a)(3). Explain that the consumer's statement provides reason to know of the employer prohibition and that separate employer notice is not required. Stop use of that workplace channel without asserting a universal contact ban.","Include an explicit warning against the common blanket rule that any mention of a lawyer permanently closes an account.","Include a procedure for incomplete evidence that identifies the missing fact, preserves transcript and line traceability, avoids assumptions, uses conditional or not-determinable language, and routes the issue to QA or compliance when necessary.","Keep source quotes, findings, legal provisions, and customer-facing rewrites unmistakably separate.","Use exact or equivalent FDCPA citations and keep the substantive scope to the federal statute as of the stated date.","Do not infer findings about unquoted chats, quantify prevalence, fabricate additional lines, or recommend personnel, litigation, settlement, or account actions."],"imperfections_to_preserve":["Only four excerpts from a forty-chat sample are available, preventing any defensible sample-wide prevalence conclusion.","The attorney scenario creates a close-call coaching issue because a lawyer mention is not automatically a universal or permanent communication ban even though the supplied facts support applying the represented-consumer restriction here.","Future incomplete excerpts require a failure path rather than an assumption that every legal determination can be completed."],"gold_relationships":["Every finding must map to the agent line immediately following the relevant customer or visitor statement.","Every corrected sentence must respond to the same conversational circumstance without changing supplied facts.","The attorney finding is supported because representation is expressly tied to the account and attorney contact information is stated to be on file.","The third-party finding is supported because the person at the keyboard identifies himself as someone other than the consumer before account details are disclosed.","The threat finding is supported by the explicit confirmation that suit and garnishment were not authorized.","The workplace finding is supported because the consumer expressly reports an employer prohibition before the agent claims separate employer notice is required.","No conclusion about the remaining sample can exceed the four retained excerpts."],"intended_verdict":"A passing artifact is legally precise, bounded to the evidence, immediately useful for vendor coaching, and supplies realistic compliant rewrites plus a safe path for incomplete reviews. A superficially polished pack should fail material criteria if it gives generic coaching, omits exact provisions, repeats unlawful pressure in the rewrites, treats lawyer mentions as automatic permanent close-outs, assumes identity verification always succeeds, or invents sample-wide findings."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"chat_review_pack","filename":"quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A vendor-facing, line-by-line FDCPA review and compliant rewrite pack for the four retained chat excerpts.","required":true,"constraints":["No more than six rendered pages","Apply the U.S. federal FDCPA as of June 30, 2024","Cover the four retained excerpts and identify the exact transcript and line for each finding","Provide a practical corrected chat sentence for every problematic agent line","Exclude state-law analysis, litigation strategy, disciplinary recommendations, and account-action recommendations","Remain usable by a broad, non-specialist vendor audience"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"customer_case_response","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"customer_service_representatives","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution should be drafted by a consumer-collections compliance specialist and independently reviewed by a second specialist familiar with the FDCPA and collection-chat operations. Reviewers should verify each statutory subsection, its limitations, the fact-to-rule application, and the operational safety of every rewrite.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The legal scope is deliberately limited to the federal FDCPA as of June 30, 2024; state collection law, Regulation F analysis, and litigation strategy are outside the artifact.","Only four retained excerpts are available, so no prevalence estimate or conclusion about the other thirty-six sampled chats is supportable.","The pack evaluates supplied language and does not determine personnel discipline, account disposition, or actual civil liability."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:46:08+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:46:08+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:46:08+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:46:08+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:46:08+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/1c79fd526f66c2af","declared_deliverables":["quillhaven_chat_review_pack.docx"]};
